<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Antigonus II Gonatas</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 320–239 BCE</span> · <a href="/centuries/3rd-century-bce">3rd century BCE</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/antigonus-i-monophthalmus">Antigonus</a> II Gonatas was king of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-macedon">Macedon</a> and son of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/demetrius-i-of-macedon">Demetrius Poliorcetes</a>. His victory over the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gauls">Gauls</a> at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lysimachia">Lysimachia</a> in 277 BCE won him the Macedonian throne, and he established the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/antigonid-dynasty">Antigonid dynasty</a> firmly in Macedon. He fought the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chremonidean-war">Chremonidean War</a> against <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/athens">Athens</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sparta">Sparta</a> and kept garrisons in key Greek cities such as Corinth.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/antigonus-ii-gonatas.jpg" alt="Antigonus II Gonatas" width="320" height="320" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Antigone II (0319-0239 av. J.-C.; roi de Macédoine). Autorité émettrice de monnaie présumée Antigonos III (0263-0221... · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Monnaie_-_T%C3%A9tradrachme,_argent,_Pella,_Mac%C3%A9doine,_Antigone_II_Gonatas_-_btv1b8500006s_(1_of_2).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
